I have written a patch to change the scoring for monster deaths. Killing 
monsters that you create/revive/re-animate with create familiar, create 
monster, turn undead, or stone to flesh will not increase your score. 
Nor will killing monsters you create from figurines, bags of tricks, 
reverse genociding, summoning were-help, or laying eggs. In addition, 
killing unique monsters only gives you points the first time they die, 
except for the wizard and the riders, which give you 1/3 less points 
each time. Trolls will give you full points for every death until you 
revive or reanimate them, and then they are worth nothing. This patch 
only affects the scoreboard; experience points are awarded for all 
monster deaths as normal.

You can download the patch at: http://michael.lehotay.com/nethack/index.html

I considered adjusting the scoring system to account for conducts, 
number of turns, and various other aspects of the game, but decided to 
leave that alone for now since there does not seem to be agreement in 
the newsgroup about how a new scoring system would work.

